  "id": "endogenous-opioid",
  "term": "endogenous opioid",
  "definition": "An endogenous opioid is a naturally produced brain chemical, such as enkephalins or beta-endorphins, that is linked here to feelings of social bondedness. In this source, endogenous opioids are described as restraining vasopressin release and as potentially contributing to effects such as social connectedness, placebo responding, and health benefits tied to close relationships.",
